# <Project> — session anchor (short on purpose; the authorities are below)

**Read before dispatching or landing anything:**

| Authority | Governs |
|---|---|
| `docs/core-model.md` + factory docs | The whole factory map |
| `docs/OPERATIONS.md` (yours, translated) | Operational law — procedure changes are reviewed diffs to this file |
| `.claude/templates/lane-brief.md` | The standing lane brief — dispatch from THIS |
| `docs/train-plan.md` | Landing commands, resource contract, landing mode (`pr` default) and the branch-policy date |
| GitHub Project «<name>» (#N, `<PROJECT_ID>`) | Forward planning source of truth |

Status field: `<STATUS_FIELD_ID>` · options: Planned=`<id>` In flight=`<id>`
Deferred=`<id>` Done=`<id>` Decision needed=`<id>` Dropped=`<id>`

## Board transaction points
| Event | Action |
|---|---|
| Work dispatched | Real issue, Status → In flight |
| Train lands | Boarded items → Done, then archive (pr mode: on merge) |
| New deferred item | File with full body, → Deferred |
| Needs owner ruling | → Decision needed |

## Non-negotiables
- <your domain's hard rules — data classification, secrets policy, etc.>
- New test literals via `secrets.token_urlsafe`.
- The choices audit is a transaction point: every lane handback → ledger
  entry in `docs/choices/<train>.md`; unsound resolved before assembly.
